{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Opened a second A2 line and submitted its experiment. Source reading: initiateLeadershipTransfer does not inspect the destination's suffrage, TimeoutNow makes any destination a candidate with the leadership-transfer flag and no pre-vote, every voter adopts that higher term and steps down before the suffrage check rejects the vote, and the transfer branch reports success through the leftLeaderLoop path without checking whether the requested destination became leader - while pickServer filters non-voters explicitly. The experiment transfers leadership in a real 4-node cluster to a demoted non-voter and, as a control, to a voter, recording the future's result, the states of the old leader and the target, whether the target ever leads, and term movement over an 8s watch. Five comparisons encode: success reported for a non-voter destination, the destination never leading, the existing leadership being removed, and the voter-destination control succeeding with the destination actually leading. Native local execution of this harness produced exactly that pattern (non-voter target: nil result, old leader Follower, target Candidate and never Leader, cluster recovering with another node leading; voter target: nil result and the target Leader), so the formal receipt should decide the claim; the interpretation follows the receipt.\"}"}}
